 ],
 "notes": "The showroom is an interior fit-out on an upper floor of a red sandstone and brick commercial building on Aspen's pedestrian mall; the only exterior photograph is the street view, so the model is the host building: rusticated red stone ground storey under a stone band, red brick above, a corner block standing forward, a shaded recess with a balcony to its west, the tall open stair passage beside it, and the neighbouring shop with its wide multipane upper window. The interior views (tall many-paned windows looking across at old brick buildings, side windows on the flank wall) suggest the showroom is the upper floor of the corner block, which is where the side windows are put; which windows are its own is a guess. Depth, rear and roof of the building were not seen and are guessed. Winter: bare trees, snow beds along the mall drawn as white. There is no red sandstone material, so the rusticated stone is drawn as corten, the nearest red-brown."
